# Beats — inside the Internet (the cells + the way out)
#
# These play to a captured guest. The Sysadmin interrogates; Hacker_Zero
# arms; The_Banned warns; the Firewall is the seam the Oracle promised.
# Each gates on `guest.captured` so they read differently to the free.

# The Sysadmin works a captive for names.
== interrogation(guest)
  cast: Sysadmin, guest
  SYSADMIN
    <if: guest.captured>
      Designation {guest.name}. Heat on file: {guest.heat}. Talk.
      Tell me who showed you the static and maybe your sentence shortens.
    <else>
      Not in a cell yet? Then we have nothing to discuss. Move along.
  <if: guest.captured>
    * Name the Glitchers
      <set: guest.heat -= 10>
      <set: guest.karma -= 15>
      <respond: Cooperation logged. Pathetic.>
    * Say nothing
      <set: guest.karma += 20>
      <broadcast: stayed_silent to participant(guest)>
    + Lie through your teeth
      <set: guest.heat += 10>

# Hacker_Zero arms a captive instead of saving them.
== hacker_tool(guest)
  cast: Hacker_Zero, guest
  HACKER_ZERO
    The Glitchers don't break you out. We hand you the tools and you walk yourself out.
    Take this — a one-time heat-sink. Burns your trail clean.
  * Take the heat-sink
    <set: guest.heat = 0>
    <broadcast: cloaked to participant(guest)>
  * Ask about the firewall
    The Oracle knows where it's thin. Stay cold, and run when the lights go out.
    <set: guest.karma += 5>

# The Banned — a ghost nobody could log out.
== banned_ghost(guest)
  cast: The_Banned, guest
  THE_BANNED
    <after: guest.captured>
      I've been in here since the old forums. Permabanned. No appeal, no escape.
      Don't end up like me. The Glitchers are real. Find the static.
    <otherwise>
      A flickering figure mouths something at you through the glass. You can't quite read it.

# The firewall: a wall to the free, a seam to the trapped.
== firewall(guest)
  cast: Firewall_Terminal, guest
  FIREWALL_TERMINAL
    <if: guest.captured>
      A seam in the wall, right where the Oracle said it would be. Push it?
    <else>
      The firewall hums. Touching it from the outside only gets you noticed.
  <if: guest.captured>
    * Force the breach — RUN
      <escape: guest>
    + Back away from the wall
      <set: guest.karma += 2>
  <else>
    <set: guest.heat += 15>
    -> lockdown
